# Status bar: exactly ONE of the two drop-ins deploys, keyed on
# features.quickshell_shell. They are mutually exclusive because the Quickshell
# bar floats (40 tall, inset 4, reserving 44) and Waybar's 30px full-bleed bar
# cannot stack with that — so autostart and the SUPER+B toggle both live in the
# drop-in rather than in conf/autostart.* and conf/bindings/desktop-utilities.*.
# Flipping the flag and running `chezmoi apply` is the whole rollout, and
# flipping it back is the whole rollback. Both Hyprland entry points glob conf.d
# and tolerate absence, so an undeployed drop-in is simply never sourced.
#
# The gate lives here rather than in the drop-ins because a .lua/.conf file
# cannot carry template actions, and .chezmoidata files cannot be templates
# (see .claude/rules/chezmoi-data.md). Status: _research/QUICKSHELL_SURFACE_INVENTORY.md
{{ if not .features.quickshell_shell.enabled }}
.config/hypr/conf.d/quickshell.lua
.config/hypr/conf.d/quickshell.conf
.config/quickshell
{{ else }}
.config/hypr/conf.d/waybar.lua
.config/hypr/conf.d/waybar.conf
{{ end }}

# Polkit agent: exactly ONE exists per session, so the Quickshell agent
# (quickshell/dotfiles/polkit/PolkitDialog.qml, behind Config.polkitOwned) and
# polkit-gnome are mutually exclusive. Its own flag rather than the bar's: the
# bar and a session-exclusive D-Bus agent are separate decisions, exactly as
# quickshell_notifications is separate for swaync. The line polkit-gnome.* holds
# used to live unconditionally in conf/autostart.*, which BOTH branches load.
{{ if .features.quickshell_polkit.enabled }}
.config/hypr/conf.d/polkit-gnome.lua
.config/hypr/conf.d/polkit-gnome.conf
{{ end }}

